WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.067
-President Biden and Senate
Democrats say

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:06.200
they'll move quickly to
appoint and confirm a successor

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.367
to retiring Supreme
Court Justice Stephen Breyer,

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:09.801
which they absolutely must

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:11.300
because if Republicans
had their way,

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.100
they'd almost certainly
keep the seat vacant

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.000
until they could
fill it themselves.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.334
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:21.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:22.901
Well, guys, it is not often

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.868
I get to report good news
on this show,

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:26.834
but things are finally
looking up for Democrats

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:28.934
because they'll have a chance
to choose a new

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:30.267
Supreme Court justice.

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:32.801
After 27 years
on the Supreme Court today,

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:34.667
we learned that
Justice Stephen Breyer,

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.334
who's 83 years old,
is retiring.

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:41.200
Justice Breyer is one of the
three remaining liberal justices

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.801
in the six-three court.

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:45.267
-I was proud and grateful
to be there at the start

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:48.033
of his distinguished career
in the Supreme Court,

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.767
and I'm very proud
to be here today

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:52.734
on his announcement
of his retirement.

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:56.100
-The overall, sort of,
ideological split on the court

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.334
will not change one iota.
It is a, generally speaking,

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:04.567
a six-to-three conservative
majority court.

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:07.501
-That's right, everyone,
liberals get to maintain

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:11.767
a three-six minority. Whoo!

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:14.300
Round of tap waters
for everyone!

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.634
Who wants tap?
We got tap from the sink.

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:20.701
Wally, breakout an appropriate
number of balloons.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:24.801
Okay. You know what?
You know what,

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:29.534
I think we can go ahead
and drop a single "confettum."

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:39.534
Try to keep an eye on it.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:45.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:47.501
We also called up DJ Khaled

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:50.534
and asked if we could borrow
his celebratory air horn.

00:01:50.534 --> 00:01:52.400
And he asked what for,
and I explained the good news

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.667
about maintaining a three to six
minority on the court.

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:57.133
And then he told me
that I played myself.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.968
And I said, "Can I have
the air horn or not?"

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:03.100
He said, "You can have a horn
appropriate to the news,

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.300
so this is what we got."

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.767
-[ Horn blares ]
-Free horn!

00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:10.667
Who played whose self now?

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:13.434
That being said, this will
still be a historic appointment

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:15.834
because today Biden reaffirmed
his commitment

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:17.667
to putting the first
Black woman on the court,

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:19.734
which is obviously a momentous
and long overdue step,

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.634
but otherwise Biden
has been pretty tight-lipped

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:23.133
about his choice.

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:25.234
Yesterday, for example,
he demurred when asked about it

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:26.834
by reporters
at a White House event

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:29.133
and jokingly asked someone
on a panel with him

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:31.667
if they wanted to join
the Supreme Court.

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:43.834
-There has been no announcement
from Justice Breyer.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:46.367
Let him make whatever statement
he's going to make,

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:48.767
and I'll be happy
to talk about it later.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:51.634
-We're going to start
by asking Tom --

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.701
Tom Linebarger -- to --
to offer your thoughts.

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:55.467
Please, sir.

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:57.133
-Thank you, Mr. President.
It's an honor to be here.

00:02:57.133 --> 00:03:00.434
-Want to go to the
Supreme Court, Tom?

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:02.100
-I'm just going to demure
on that one.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.934
-Hey, man, don't joke around
like that,

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:07.868
because that's absolutely
how Trump picked Kavanaugh.

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.267
[As Trump]
We need a Supreme Court justice.

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:11.133
Hey, you.
You, with the beer bong.

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:13.634
You want to be
on the Supreme Court?

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:16.434
[As Kavanaugh]
Who, me or my buddy Squee?!

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:17.801
[Normal voice]
And I'm just joking.

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.067
He wasn't chosen randomly.

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:21.400
Trump was given a list
by The Federalist Society,

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.133
which is a shadowy
group of conservatives

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:25.067
who secretly control the levers
of power in this country

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:26.934
when Republicans are in office.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:29.033
You know what, Wally?
Get rid of that one balloon.

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:32.634
[ Air screeches out of balloon ]

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:34.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.667
Did you strangle it?

00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:41.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:43.200
And then today, Biden appeared
at the White House

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.367
alongside Breyer to officially
announce Breyer's retirement

00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:48.834
but made clear to reporters
he would not take questions.

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:50.200
-I'm not going to take
any questions

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.868
because I think
it's inappropriate

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:55.000
to take questions
with the Justice here.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.434
He's still sitting
on the bench,

00:03:56.434 --> 00:03:58.467
but you'll have plenty
of opportunities

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:00.234
to get me later today

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:02.534
and for the rest of the week,
next week, too.

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:05.067
So thank you very much.
Thank you.

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:08.634
[ Reporters shouting questions ]

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:13.634
-And thank goodness this time

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:16.167
President Biden made sure
to walk away from the microphone

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:18.400
because we all know
what happens when he doesn't.

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.267
Here, though. Here --

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:34.534
Here's my question about that.

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:37.567
Did he really think
no one would hear him?

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:39.534
I mean, even if the mic
wasn't there,

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:41.200
you're still in a room
full of people.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.968
You're surrounded by report--
You're on camera!

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:45.601
Even if Biden just
mouthed the words,

00:04:45.601 --> 00:04:47.434
I'm pretty sure
we could've read his lips.

00:04:47.434 --> 00:04:48.601
Like, watch my mouth.

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:53.834
I think you can tell what I just
said. Even without the words,

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:56.300
his expression says,
"You stupid son of a bitch."

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.501 --> 00:05:01.133
Forget the hot mic,
Biden's got a hot face.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:02.634
So before today's
official announcement,

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:04.601
Biden and his aides
were walking on eggshells

00:05:04.601 --> 00:05:05.934
and trying to be
respectful of Breyer

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:07.834
because in our dumb system,

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:09.100
there was nothing
stopping Breyer

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.934
from just changing his mind
and sticking around.

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:12.501
And we all have to just nod
and pretend

00:05:12.501 --> 00:05:14.100
that having a forever job
this important

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.567
isn't totally [bleep] crazy.

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:17.968
I mean, what about
an employee review every decade?

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:19.300
Is that too much to ask?

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.334
Whoever came up with the idea
of lifetime appointments

00:05:21.334 --> 00:05:23.634
must have been a --
-Stupid son of a bitch.

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:26.300
-But regardless of Biden
playing coy,

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.834
he and Senate Democrats
have made clear

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:31.234
that they plan to move fast
to confirm Breyer's successor.

00:05:31.234 --> 00:05:33.033
Senate Majority Leader
Chuck Schumer

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:36.167
said the Senate would move with
"all deliberate speed."

00:05:36.167 --> 00:05:37.601
Although forgive me
if I don't trust

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:39.100
Senate Democrats
to move quickly.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.667
No one who wears
their glasses like this

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:45.400
is known for their urgency.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.501
In ophthalmology,
they call that glasses position

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:50.234
the "hold your horses."

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:52.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.434
Schumer looks like he's sampling

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:56.567
every flavor at a Baskin-Robbins
before ordering.

00:05:56.567 --> 00:05:58.634
[As Schumer] And now let me try
a little of the Rocky Road.

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:00.934
This is getting harder,
not easier.

00:06:04.901 --> 00:06:07.267
I hope the people behind me
haven't been waiting too long.

00:06:07.267 --> 00:06:08.567
Oh, dear!

00:06:09.534 --> 00:06:11.734
[Normal voice]
Still, Democrats --

00:06:11.734 --> 00:06:14.300
Still, Democrats
seem aware of the urgency

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:15.501
and the need to move quickly

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:17.167
because Republicans
have repeatedly implied

00:06:17.167 --> 00:06:19.267
or said outright
that if they had their way,

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:20.934
they would hold the seat hostage

00:06:20.934 --> 00:06:22.968
and keep it empty
until a Republican can fill it.

00:06:22.968 --> 00:06:25.868
That's their position now
and was their position in 2016,

00:06:25.868 --> 00:06:28.634
when Republicans, including
Ted Cruz and Donald Trump,

00:06:28.634 --> 00:06:32.100
infamously said they would never
confirm a Democratic nominee,

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.667
no matter what year it was.

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:36.367
-You've said that the president
shouldn't nominate anyone

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:39.667
in the rest of his term
to replace Justice Scalia.

00:06:39.667 --> 00:06:41.234
-I think it's up
to Mitch McConnell

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:45.167
and everybody else to stop it.
It's called delay, delay, delay.

00:06:45.167 --> 00:06:46.934
-Sounds like the one guy
at a soccer match

00:06:46.934 --> 00:06:48.934
who doesn't quite know
how to do the chant.

00:06:48.934 --> 00:06:51.901
"Olé, olé, olé, oh --
-Delay delay.

00:06:51.901 --> 00:06:53.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.968 --> 00:06:55.467
That was in 2016,

00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:57.367
but it won't surprise you to
learn that nothing has changed.

00:06:57.367 --> 00:06:59.934
Mitch McConnell has already said
he likely wouldn't confirm

00:06:59.934 --> 00:07:01.968
a Biden nominee in 2024,

00:07:01.968 --> 00:07:03.667
if Republicans win
back the Senate,

00:07:03.667 --> 00:07:05.868
and left the door open
to stonewalling a nominee

00:07:05.868 --> 00:07:08.801
in 2023, as well, saying,
"Cross those bridges

00:07:08.801 --> 00:07:10.701
when I get there,
we're focusing on '22."

00:07:10.701 --> 00:07:14.167
I don't rule anything in or out
about how to handle nominations

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:15.601
if I'm in the majority position.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.067
You can't even
bring yourself to say

00:07:17.067 --> 00:07:19.868
that you'd consider
a president's Supreme Court pick

00:07:19.868 --> 00:07:21.100
in a non-election year.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:22.400
So what's your position then?

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:25.400
Only Republicans
are allowed to govern?

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:28.234
Oh, that is their position?
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.234 --> 00:07:29.701
But then that wouldn't be
a democracy, right?

00:07:29.701 --> 00:07:35.334
Well, what would it be?
Oh, well, that's not good.

00:07:35.334 --> 00:07:37.300
If McConnell got his way,
Biden's only job

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.300
would be grilling hot dogs,
eating ice cream,

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:42.367
and giving people finger guns
at the State of the Union.

00:07:42.367 --> 00:07:45.100
And that right there -- that
right there is the difference

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:47.067
between being vice president
and being president.

00:07:47.067 --> 00:07:50.601
Vice president, it's like riding
shotgun on a road trip,

00:07:50.601 --> 00:07:52.501
just messing with the radio,

00:07:52.501 --> 00:07:54.767
winking at the girls
in other cars,

00:07:54.767 --> 00:07:59.033
doing that hand thing
with the wind.

00:07:59.033 --> 00:08:00.734
But now that he's the one
driving, he's all,

00:08:00.734 --> 00:08:04.400
"Everybody shut up!
I'm trying to concentrate!

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:08.300
Can I get over there?!
Our exit's coming up!"

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.400
Several GOP senators went
even further than McConnell,

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:13.567
telling CNN they would oppose
any Biden nominee,

00:08:13.567 --> 00:08:14.801
no matter what year it is.

00:08:14.801 --> 00:08:16.434
Iowa senator Chuck Grassley,

00:08:16.434 --> 00:08:18.868
the ranking Republican
on the Judiciary Committee,

00:08:18.868 --> 00:08:20.267
even went so far as to make up

00:08:20.267 --> 00:08:22.701
another totally
nonexistent rule, telling CNN...

00:08:30.667 --> 00:08:33.534
First of all, don't tell us
to go back to 1886

00:08:33.534 --> 00:08:36.334
just because
you go back to 1886.

00:08:36.334 --> 00:08:38.000
I'm not saying Grassley's old,

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.701
but his first campaign
was for president of Pangaea.

00:08:41.701 --> 00:08:44.667
"Only I can keep us together!"

00:08:44.667 --> 00:08:47.901
Second, there's no such rule.

00:08:47.901 --> 00:08:49.267
As CNN noted...

00:09:02.501 --> 00:09:04.601
Do you think we can't
just look this stuff up,

00:09:04.601 --> 00:09:06.367
or have you just not heard
about Google

00:09:06.367 --> 00:09:08.567
and think we have to go
to the library to find it?

00:09:08.567 --> 00:09:11.834
"Have fun going through
microfiche, ya losers!"

00:09:11.834 --> 00:09:13.634
And that's not a joke
about Chuck Grassley

00:09:13.634 --> 00:09:15.067
being too old
to know about Google.

00:09:15.067 --> 00:09:17.267
That's a joke about Grassley
being bad at technology,

00:09:17.267 --> 00:09:19.300
like the time
he tweeted out of nowhere

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:20.968
with no additional context...

00:09:24.868 --> 00:09:26.901
[ Laughter ]

00:09:31.067 --> 00:09:32.801
I'm so relieved
we found that tweet.

00:09:32.801 --> 00:09:35.400
One of our interns spent all day
looking through the stacks

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:38.734
at the Twitter Library
in Long Island City.

00:09:38.734 --> 00:09:42.467
They found that
and the deer carcass.

00:09:42.467 --> 00:09:44.934
So clearly these guys
just make [bleep] up as they go.

00:09:44.934 --> 00:09:46.367
You know, the same way
your mom does

00:09:46.367 --> 00:09:48.868
which she has too much gin
during a game of Monopoly.

00:09:48.868 --> 00:09:51.367
"Mom, you can't put a hotel
on a railroad!"

00:09:51.367 --> 00:09:55.300
[Slurring] "Well, where are
the people supposed to stay?

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:57.234
You know, while they wait
for their train.

00:09:57.234 --> 00:09:59.567
I'll bet there's a nice bar
in that little hotel."

00:09:59.567 --> 00:10:00.968
"You have a problem, Mother!"

00:10:00.968 --> 00:10:05.000
"Well, that, I better call
Dr. Hendrick's."

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.801
There's no reason
to ever take seriously

00:10:06.801 --> 00:10:08.467
anything these guys say
ever again.

00:10:08.467 --> 00:10:10.634
They blocked President Obama's
Supreme Court nominee

00:10:10.634 --> 00:10:12.133
eight months before an election

00:10:12.133 --> 00:10:14.634
and then rushed to confirm
Amy Coney Barrett

00:10:14.634 --> 00:10:16.300
eight days before an election.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:18.968
Now they're saying, even when
it's not an election year,

00:10:18.968 --> 00:10:20.868
they won't confirm
a Democratic nominee.

00:10:20.868 --> 00:10:23.367
Next, McConnell is going to
claim the Constitution says...

00:10:31.501 --> 00:10:34.000
This is why Breyer
had to retire now --

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.834
so Democrats could replace him

00:10:35.834 --> 00:10:38.100
before Republicans potentially
win back the Senate in November.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:40.334
And to help nudge Breyer
toward retirement,

00:10:40.334 --> 00:10:42.501
there's been a sustained
pressure campaign

00:10:42.501 --> 00:10:43.634
from progressives.

00:10:43.634 --> 00:10:45.100
-It is clear
that the court's future

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:47.434
is really his main reason
for leaving

00:10:47.434 --> 00:10:49.734
after almost three decades
on the court.

00:10:49.734 --> 00:10:52.734
He has spoken extensively,
particularly over the past year.

00:10:52.734 --> 00:10:54.634
He even wrote a book
that was released

00:10:54.634 --> 00:10:55.801
in September.

00:10:55.801 --> 00:10:57.534
And in those speeches,
in his book,

00:10:57.534 --> 00:11:00.200
he expressed concern
that the public views

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:02.000
the court as political

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.868
and he talks about
how that perception

00:11:03.868 --> 00:11:06.167
could really erode faith
in the court.

00:11:06.167 --> 00:11:09.701
He understands this relentless,
over the past year,

00:11:09.701 --> 00:11:12.601
progressive pressure on him
to step down.

00:11:12.601 --> 00:11:16.467
In fact, the progressive group
Demand Justice just last spring,

00:11:16.467 --> 00:11:19.634
they paraded a mobile billboard
past the Supreme Court

00:11:19.634 --> 00:11:22.067
with the simple words
"Breyer, retire,"

00:11:22.067 --> 00:11:24.133
trying to get
their message out there.

00:11:24.133 --> 00:11:26.133
-I have to say I enjoy the idea
of paying

00:11:26.133 --> 00:11:28.634
for a mobile billboard
that targets one guy.

00:11:28.634 --> 00:11:32.501
It's like seeing an ad on
the side of a bus that says...

00:11:42.067 --> 00:11:45.400
Also, can we please dispense
with this ridiculous fiction

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:47.033
that the court somehow
isn't political?

00:11:47.033 --> 00:11:48.467
That's all it is.

00:11:48.467 --> 00:11:51.133
They want all of us to act
like it's the Jedi Council

00:11:51.133 --> 00:11:53.968
soberly deliberating over
what's best for the galaxy

00:11:53.968 --> 00:11:56.334
when it's really just a group
of Republicans and Democrats

00:11:56.334 --> 00:11:58.400
nominated by Republicans
and Democrats who do the things

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.467
Republicans and Democrats
want them to do.

00:12:00.467 --> 00:12:02.167
Pretending the court
isn't political

00:12:02.167 --> 00:12:04.601
is like pretending
reality-show casts are assembled

00:12:04.601 --> 00:12:07.567
for the purposes of
having drama-free interactions.

00:12:07.567 --> 00:12:10.100
"I don't know
where we went wrong

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:11.801
with this season
of 'Real Housewives,'

00:12:11.801 --> 00:12:16.501
but some of these ladies
do not get along!"

00:12:16.501 --> 00:12:18.801
This is an opportunity
for Biden and Democrats

00:12:18.801 --> 00:12:20.467
to make a historic impact
on the court

00:12:20.467 --> 00:12:22.701
by confirming the first
Black woman in U.S. history,

00:12:22.701 --> 00:12:24.701
a move that is both momentous
and long overdue.

00:12:24.701 --> 00:12:26.701
But it says a lot
about our current politics

00:12:26.701 --> 00:12:29.033
that if Breyer hadn't retired
now, there's a good chance

00:12:29.033 --> 00:12:30.968
Republicans would have held
the seat hostage

00:12:30.968 --> 00:12:32.934
and never let Biden
nominate anyone,

00:12:32.934 --> 00:12:34.601
which, if you ask me,
is pretty...

00:12:34.601 --> 00:12:37.000
-Stupid.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:38.968
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:38.968 --> 00:12:42.200
♪♪

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.567
God's Love We Deliver cooks
and brings over two million

00:12:44.567 --> 00:12:46.534
meals a year to men, women,
and children

00:12:46.534 --> 00:12:49.234
living with HIV/AIDS, cancer,
and other serious illnesses,

00:12:49.234 --> 00:12:50.734
and they need your help now
more than ever.

00:12:50.734 --> 00:12:52.734
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the donate button.

00:12:52.734 --> 00:12:55.467
Stay safe. Get vaccinated.
We love you.

